2739 tool: {"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-reasoning", "file": "references/failed-periodic-guess-reassessment.md", "content": "# Reassessing a failed periodic-color guess\n\nWhen a periodic-color submission is rejected, do not simply swap colors or tweak the checkerboard phase. Audit the rule at the representation level:\n\n1. Separate the observed palette from the spatial encoding. A test with two visible colors does not establish that the output alternates those colors; sparse marker positions may encode only the phase, direction, or offsets of a richer latent cycle learned from a demo.\n2. Compare geometry, not just colors: inspect diagonal/parallel tracks, coordinate offsets, motif repetition, and row/column phase progression. Ask whether these features can index a sequence seen in the demo.\n3. Reconstruct and validate the candidate across all demonstrated cells/rows before applying it to the test. An elegant motif that fits one interpretation is not enough if another encoding remains plausible.\n4. If the unresolved interpretations predict different outputs, request a strategically informative demo instead of making a speculative second submission. Stop requesting when the rule is sufficiently grounded.\n5. Preserve the one-action benchmark protocol; a wrong submission calls for one revised action, never commentary followed by an action.\n\nThis is a general caution for cross-encoding periodic tasks, not a claim that every diagonal-marker grid encodes a color cycle this way. Pair it with `references/cross-encoding-demo-uncertainty.md` and `references/post-error-reassessment.md`.\n", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544721/attempts/cad7481303e4469588333dc46b5ca8fd/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-reasoning/references/failed-periodic-guess-reassessment.md"}

