2758 tool: {"success": true, "name": "arc-periodic-color-structure", "file": "references/cross-encoding-cycle-inference.md", "content": "# Cross-encoding periodic cycle inference\n\nA set of demos may encode a periodic output in very different input forms: full-width bands, sparse diagonal traces, or repeating motifs. The output may have a clear minimal period even when the input-to-cycle mapping is not yet clear. Separate cycle identification from rule inference.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Record input cues and positions independently: for horizontal bands, list each stripe's color and row; for sparse traces, record their diagonal residue/offset and color; for repeated motifs, note ordering and repetitions.\n2. Record the output's minimal color sequence, orientation, and starting phase separately. Do not collapse period, order, and phase into a single guess.\n3. Test candidate input-to-output mappings (encounter order, spatial order, rotations, reversals, repeated-color treatment, or residue-based indexing) against every demo, including the transition at the repeat boundary.\n4. Apply a mapping to a differently encoded test only if the demos support that cross-encoding correspondence. Matching palette alone does not establish the sequence or phase.\n5. If candidate mappings predict different test grids, request a demo designed to distinguish them. After a rejected submission, audit the entire selector/order/phase rule rather than trying a local color or row change.\n\nA periodic-looking candidate must explain every demonstration's output sequence and every test cue used to choose its order and phase.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544721/attempts/cad7481303e4469588333dc46b5ca8fd/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-periodic-color-structure/references/cross-encoding-cycle-inference.md"}

